## Lens coverage

| Lens | Coverage | Residual limitation |
|---|---|---|
| 8B.1 | Strong | Ideology and goals are clear, but some derive from inherited CPV doctrine. |
| 8B.2 | Strong | Priorities, institutions, work programs, and numeric enforcement targets are documented; granular budget attribution to Trọng is absent. |
| 8B.3 | Strong | Nationwide party and anti-corruption mobilization is visible; much evidence is official. |
| 8B.4 | Partial | Appointments and removal mechanisms are visible, but independent evidence evaluating appointee competence in 2022 is insufficient. |
| 8B.5 | Moderate | Central and provincial coordination is documented, counterbalanced by World Bank implementation weaknesses. |
| 8B.6 | Strong | Provincial rollout and active case management show state reach; economic-program execution was incomplete. |
| 8B.7 | Moderate | Outcomes moved favorably, but causal attribution is confounded by reopening, exports, inherited fundamentals, and collective government action. |
| 8B.8 | Moderate | Explicit correction doctrine and closing of institutional loopholes are documented; measured results of tactical adaptation remain thin. |
| 8B.9 | Strong | China relations and wider strategic balancing were actively managed, although under significant constraints. |
| 8B.10 | Moderate | Anti-corruption reach, regime control, diplomatic access, and recovery advanced; durability and personal causation cannot be resolved from one year. |

## Search accounting

- Plausible documents discovered: 34
- Underlying documents/pages opened: 14
- Accepted source-claim units: 11
- Reused units verified: 3
- Newly accepted units: 8
- Rejected after inspection: 17
- Access-blocked or fetch-failed: 3
- Discovery-only/unopened after triage: 3
- Distinct accepted-source organizations: 7
- Accepted source types: official transcript, official government reporting, multilateral assessment, peer-reviewed scholarship, and specialist foreign-policy analysis

Rejected materials were principally duplicate government stories, post-period retrospectives that added no distinct 2022 fact, search snippets without accessible underlying content, low-authority aggregators, and sources addressing other rulers or later outcomes.

The local runner was unavailable, so `research-ledger-manifest.json` could neither be inspected nor updated. The eleven physical `SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON` records above constitute the merge-ready manifest delta containing all prior records known from the supplied index plus this turn’s new records; unknown earlier ledger entries cannot safely be reconstructed or claimed as cumulative.

A further Chapter-8B-specific wave would have limited but nonzero value. The principal remaining target would be independent evidence on 2022 appointment competence and measured course correction under 8B.4 and 8B.8. Another broad search is unlikely to materially change the chapter; a focused archival search of Politburo personnel decisions, National Assembly budget execution records, and Vietnamese-language provincial implementation audits might narrow those two residual gaps.
